# Quantar custom-operator extension.
#
# `hatch_build.py` (via lang_systems.build_parser) splices this onto the vendored
# CPython grammar (Grammar/python.gram) and generates lang_systems/quantar_parser.py.
# Everything below is the *only* quantum-specific grammar; the whole rest of
# Python is inherited, so quantar is a strict superset of Python.
#
# Operators are matched against the `quantar.operators` registry at runtime, in
# two forms (see lang_systems/quantar.py):
#
#   symbolic    a  <->  b        matched by QUANTUM_OP   (lang_systems/quantar_tokens.py)
#   identifier  a  CNOT  b       matched by QUANTUM_NAME (any registered NAME)
#
# Precedence: custom operators bind *between* `comparison` and `bitwise_or`.
# lang_systems.build_parser rewires `comparison: a=quantum_expr ...`; to move the
# level, change that one splice and the rule living here. The resulting order,
# loosest to tightest, is:
#
#   or > and > not > comparisons > quantum_operator > | ^ & << >> > + - > * / ...

quantum_expr[expr_ty]:
    | a=quantum_expr quantum_operator b=bitwise_or
    | bitwise_or

quantum_operator[expr_ty]:
    | QUANTUM_OP
    | QUANTUM_NAME
